  "lineage": "Funeral and celebratory dance music of the Akan, most associated with Asante around Kumasi and documented by J. H. Kwabena Nketia. A lead singer and women's chorus alternate with an ensemble of atumpan talking drums, petia and apentemma hand drums, a donno hourglass drum and the dawuro iron bell, the dancers' gestures answering the drum language; a generic bell card stands in for the dawuro.",
